WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.480
PAVLOS PROTOPAPAS: Every single
minute, computers across the world

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.450
collect millions of gigabytes of data.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.750
What can you do to make sense
of this mountain of data?

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.830
How do data scientists process
this wealth of information

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.060
and use it in the applications
that power our modern world?

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.000
Data is the fuel for the digital age.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.630
It powers machine learning
and artificial intelligence.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:30.120
Data scientists use this fuel to conduct
research, find results, and communicate

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:30.930
their findings.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.040
You will leverage the power of
Python and apply to real life data

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.300
science problems.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.450
You will explore applications
in various domains,

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.990
hone your intuition for the
theory underlying these methods,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:48.120
and consider different ways of verifying
your models to identify and reduce

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.590
potential biases.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.260
Job prospects for data
scientists are growing.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.440
And the knowledge and skills
gained from these courses

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.790
will open up your world to machine
learning and artificial intelligence.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.260
Learn data science.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.810
And process the fuel that
powers our modern world.

